e table, there are $4$ players (James, Daniel, Thomas, David) whose age is $10$ or more years.\n\nThere are $2$ students (Robert, Charles)  whose age is less than $10$ years.\n\nSo the ratio of students whose age is $10$ or more years to those whose age is less than $10$ years is $4:2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-eeb02d6e-8ae6-56ea-8e46-b63ca4cc6db9"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-eeb02d6e-8ae6-56ea-8e46-b63ca4cc6db9" :answer-field/id #uuid "eeb02d6e-8ae6-56ea-8e46-b63ca4cc6db9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-3b7dc8ef-444b-59c5-80bc-464ad117b3f0" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e727dea5-3462-5dfd-9a17-7ba2367a662a" "answer-da2c95ee-7200-5df0-9e71-fabe2b33a6cb" "answer-3b7dc8ef-444b-59c5-80bc-464ad117b3f0" "answer-b9a32066-d0ef-5542-9af3-3b18d1635a51" "answer-b9955b54-2392-538c-83f8-d4086ddc6df8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e727dea5-3462-5dfd-9a17-7ba2367a662a" :answer/id #uuid "e727dea5-3462-5dfd-9a17-7ba2367a662a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2:4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-da2c95ee-7200-5df0-9e71-fabe2b33a6cb" :answer/id #uuid "da2c95ee-7200-5df0-9e71-fabe2b33a6cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3:4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3b7dc8ef-444b-59c5-80bc-464ad117b3f0" :answer/id #uuid "3b7dc8ef-444b-59c5-80bc-464ad117b3f0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4:2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9a32066-d0ef-5542-9af3-3b18d1635a51" :answer/id #uuid "b9a32066-d0ef-5542-9af3-3b18d1635a51" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4:3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9955b54-2392-538c-83f8-d4086ddc6df8" :answer/id #uuid "b9955b54-2392-538c-83f8-d4086ddc6df8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4:6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-342633b7-0af2-5736-9e7c-f7ff7859c8c8" :question/id #uuid "342633b7-0af2-5736-9e7c-f7ff7859c8c8" :question/math-academy-id "q-235954" :question/problem "Matt decides to distribute some candy to his best friends. The following table shows the number of candies each of his friends received. \n\n| Friends | Rose | Peter | Adriana | Vanessa | Helen | Luis | Jason |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Candies | $5$ | $6$ | $10$ | $9$ | $4$ | $3$ | $6$ |\n\n$$\n\n$$\n\nWhat is the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy?\n\nThe required ratio is{{field-1}}\n$:$\n{{field-2}}" :question/worked-solution "From the table, there are $2$ friends (Adriana and Vanessa) who received at least $8$ candies.\n\nOn the other hand, there are $5$ friends (Rose, Peter, Helen, Luis, and Jason) who received less than $8$ candies.\n\nSo the ratio of friends who received at least $8$ pieces of candy to those who received less than $8$ pieces of candy is $2:5.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d321aa09-ec71-546b-b682-5ccdea2fdee7" "answer-field-1e649824-e4c4-50c3-8fea-b8d2c9ca222e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d321aa09-ec71-546b-b682-5ccdea2fdee7" :answer-field/id #uuid "d321aa09-ec71-546b-b682-5ccdea2fdee7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-b4307f52-b543-51d7-aded-475a68b839c9" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b4307f52-b543-51d7-aded-475a68b839c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b4307f52-b543-51d7-aded-475a68b839c9" :answer/id #uuid "b4307f52-b543-51d7-aded-475a68b839c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1e649824-e4c4-50c3-8fea-b8d2c9ca222e" :answer-field/id #uuid "1e649824-e4c4-50c3-8fea-b8d2c9ca222e" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "answer-27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54" :answer/id #uuid "27ec799c-450f-552a-a2ad-1089fce23f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-02447e62-a41a-5aec-b911-74025102ad42" :question/id #uuid "02447e62-a41a-5aec-b911-74025102ad42" :question/math-academy-id "q-60096" :question/problem "The ratio of boys to the total number of children in a birthday party is $4:7.$ What is the meaning of this ratio?" :question/worked-solution "If the ratio of boys to total children is $4:7,$ it means that there are $4$ boys for every $7$ children at the birthday party.\n\nAnother way of writing this is to say that \"out of every $7$ children at the birthday party, $4$ of them are boys.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-f41511bf-d7bf-5d58-801e-068f8384039f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-f41511bf-d7bf-5d58-801e-068f8384039f" :answer-field/id #uuid "f41511bf-d7bf-5d58-801e-068f8384039f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f6f9e0f4-1874-5019-aaba-a4f30a494202" :answer-field/choices ["answer-aa160998-bfeb-53af-a572-22433a23e972" "answer-f6f9e0f4-1874-5019-aaba-a4f30a494202" "answer-88b20f1e-4dbe-54cd-875d-198bbcbf9920" "answer-dfc23c65-e572-5319-a310-a11bb3e8eca7" "answer-0b18d8df-3fc8-5d58-a9fd-1e8f50306474"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aa160998-bfeb-53af-a572-22433a23e972" :answer/id #uuid "aa160998-bfeb-53af-a572-22433a23e972" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Out of every $4$ children at the birthday party, $7$ of them are boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f6f9e0f4-1874-5019-aaba-a4f30a494202" :answer/id #uuid "f6f9e0f4-1874-5019-aaba-a4f30a494202" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "Out of every $7$ children at the birthday party, $4$ of them are boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88b20f1e-4dbe-54cd-875d-198bbcbf9920" :answer/id #uuid "88b20f1e-4dbe-54cd-875d-198bbcbf9920" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The birthday party has exactly $11$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfc23c65-e572-5319-a310-a11bb3e8eca7" :answer/id #uuid "dfc23c65-e572-5319-a310-a11bb3e8eca7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The birthday party has exactly $4$ boys" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b18d8df-3fc8-5d58-a9fd-1e8f50306474" :answer/id #uuid "0b18d8df-3fc8-5d58-a9fd-1e8f50306474" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "The birthday party has exactly $7$ children" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-86a8860d-3cfb-576b-a5c9-f9833c8b5308" :question/id #uuid "86a8860d-3cfb-576b-a5c9-f9833c8b5308" :question/math-academy-id "q-101428" :question/problem "![](images/7b/7b309bd6e44f1a1bc2e179dbcf50e6672366f69be364ae55b482cea16c680553.png)\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing numbers in the statement below?\n\nThe ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:\\boxed{}\\,$ because there are $\\,\\boxed{}\\,$ hexagons for every $1$ pentagon." :question/worked-solution "We can express the ratio of the number of hexagons to the number of pentagons as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of hexagons}:\\text{number of pentagons}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of hexagons. There are $4$ hexagons.\n\n- Next, we count the number of pentagons. There is $1$ pentagon.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of hexagons to pentagons is $4:1.$\n\nSo, the missing numbers are  $1$ and $4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-d752cf3e-67b8-5dd7-89f8-641e31fffc3e"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-d752cf3e-67b8-5dd7-8